<title>LUXEMBOURG: EU allocates 1997 herring quota.</title>
<headline>EU allocates 1997 herring quota.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fisheries ministers agreed on Tuesday, despite British and Portuguese objections, on the allocation of a 130,000 tonnes 1997 catch quota for Atlanto-Scandian herring, Dutch Fisheries Minister Jozias Van Aartsen said.</p>
<p>Agreement was needed before fishing for this herring species starts on May 1.</p>
<p>&quot;Otherwise fishing would have been anarchic and might have to be stopped prematurely,&quot; Van Aartsen told a news conference after a two-day Fish Council.</p>
<p>The quota was allocated as follows. Denmark 45,500 tonnes (35 percent), Germany 7,500 tonnes (5.77 percent), France 1,500 tonnes (1.15 percent), Ireland 12,000 tonnes (9.23 percent), Netherlands 17,670 tonnes (13.59 percent), Sweden 18,980 tonnes (14.60 percent), Britain 25,800 tonnes (19.85 percent), Finland 700 tonnes (0.54 percent), Portugal 150 tonnes (0.12 percent), Spain 150 tonnes (0.12 percent), Belgium 50 tonnes (0.04 percent).</p>
<p>A horse mackerel quota will be allocated at a future EU Fish Council.</p>
</text>
